    4. Place all rectangles on the grid with >=1 bg gap between bboxes; use rejection or greedy packing. Fill=1 everywhere except marker positions.
    5. Scatter marker pixels randomly within each rectangle's area.
    6. Output = crop of the winner rectangle.
